      "returncode": 0,
      "stdout": "{\"signature_verified\": true, \"payload_hash_verified\": true, \"executing_verified_fd\": true}\nTwinet builds and operates a mini-Internet: every student group runs a\nreal autonomous system with FRR, BGP, OSPF, RPKI and Open vSwitch, spread\nacross a cluster and graded automatically.\n\nUsage:\n  twinet [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  behaviour   Start and stop the scripted perturbations an exercise is built around\n  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell\n  deploy      Deploy the lab, converging whatever is already running\n  destroy     Remove every container and overlay object belonging to the lab\n  events      Show structured cluster events for a lab\n  exec        Run a command in one device or across many\n  fault       Inject, verify and resolve network faults\n  gateway     Run the SSH gateway students reach their devices through\n  grade       Grade student work against a rubric\n  graph       Render the topology as a graph\n  help        Help about any command\n  images      Create and verify reproducible image locks\n  incident    Run a reproducible network incident for agent evaluation\n  inspect     Show the expanded topology\n  msc         Operate a single-worker MSC IPsec/IPsec appliance lab\n  node        Inspect and manage the cluster's node agents\n  recover     Resume and verify a failed cluster transaction\n  restore     Load saved submissions back into a running lab\n  runtime     Machine-readable operations for an external evaluation harness\n  save        Collect each group's work into a submission archive\n  schema      Emit the manifest's JSON Schema, generated from the Go types\n  validate    Check a lab manifest and report every problem at once\n  version     Print the twinet version\n  web         Serve the connectivity matrix and looking glass for a lab\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help                    help for twinet\n      --json                    emit machine-readable JSON\n  -m, --manifest string         path to the lab manifest or its directory (default \".\")\n      --runtime string          override the manifest's container runtime for every node (docker, podman, containerd; or set TWINET_RUNTIME)\n      --runtime-socket string   endpoint for the overridden runtime (or set TWINET_RUNTIME_SOCKET)\n  -v, --verbose                 verbose logging\n\nUse \"twinet [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n",
